[size=5]Cartur's Cooking[/size]

More from the Cooking skill you already have. Food remembers who cooked it, and a better cook's food fills you up more. From level 50 a meal can come out perfect - and a perfect meal makes you Happy.

Inspired by [b]Smoothbrain's Cooking[/b] (retired in 2026), by Smoothbrain and [url=https://github.com/blaxxun-boop/Cooking]blaxxun-boop[/url] - credit to them for the idea and the design. This is a separate mod written for Valheim 1.0.

[size=4]What it does[/size]

Everything builds on the game's own Cooking skill. There is no second skill to grind, and the game's own Cooking bonuses - faster cooking and the chance of an extra portion - are kept.

[list]
[*][b]Better food[/b] - food carries the level of whoever cooked it. At 100 it gives 30% more health, stamina, health regen and eitr.
[*][b]Perfect meals[/b] - from level 50 a meal can turn out perfect (your level minus 50, in percent). Eating one makes you [b]Happy[/b]: 10% faster for 3 minutes.
[*][b]Stacks[/b] - food from different cooks stays in separate stacks, levels rounded to steps of 5.
[*][b]Kept on death[/b] - Cooking is not lowered when you die.
[*][b]Experience[/b] - 5 Cooking experience for taking food off a station; cauldron and oven meals give 5x the usual.
[/list]

[size=4]Multiplayer[/size]

Install it on the server too and its numbers apply to everyone.

Source: [url=https://github.com/jekkle/cartur-cooking]github.com/jekkle/cartur-cooking[/url]

